# Level 5's end boss and the game's ending as the original runs them: as
# level5-objs.exp (levels 1 to 4 won at their frames 20, 30, 40 and 50, the
# ship kept alive, the shops skipped but for level 5's end shop), and once
# the end boss is made ($E11) the ship moved by the stick (the game's stick
# byte $A00, written every 16 frames): down then up with fire for 256
# frames each, to bring the boss's lower half into view and back, left and
# right in turns of 32 frames, to sweep its width; at level 5's frame 9000
# the parts still standing are taken as destroyed ($D90 cleared) so the
# core can be hurt, and from then on the ship is held under it, firing (x
# 152, the fire latch $A01 set; the stick down while the world line is
# under 280, centred over 320, so the core stays on the screen). Logged as level5-objs.exp, and every update as
# it starts of the end boss $4FF7E, its parts $4FF62 and its core $4FF6E,
# with their +94 (the fire rates the allocator leaves as they
# were). Fire pressed every 30 s for each level's GET READY, the screen
# taken every 5 s; when the ending begins ($10792) Hatari leaves fast
# forward.
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage level2-jump.ini
stage level5-boss-start.ini
stage level5-frame.ini
stage level5-ending.ini
stage level5-down-left.ini
stage level5-down-right.ini
stage level5-up-left.ini
stage level5-up-right.ini
stage level5-bare.ini
stage level5-core.ini
stage level5-core-hold.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage level5-boss-obj.ini
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here, outside any hit, then clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b pc = $15
debug b pc = $16
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/level5-boss-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 2
fire
